  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Country Blues** (1 other source): Billy played this one alone, accompanied only by his banjo [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **04 Robin Built a Nest on Daddy's Grave**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Midnight On The Highway**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Country Blues**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **How Mountain Girls Do Love**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Rosa Lee McFall**: rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **Dusty Miller**: back after 51 archived shows (429 days) [3]\n- **Keep On The Sunny Side Of Life**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Brain Damage**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2021-11-16.CAPTGREG.FLAC24** (recommended): audience recording; 24 songs; 128 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: The uploader says the State Theatre has great acoustics, which helps the recording; The listener calls the capture excellent in quality and agrees the State Theatre's acoustics are great [1][2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The uploader found the State Theatre staff excellent to deal with during the taping [1]\n- The listener thinks this second night topped the first night's show [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2021-11-16.CAPTGREG.FLAC24**: taped by Capt. Greg; transferred by Capt. Greg; source: AUD [1]",
